 "about_text": "The Hammer Museum is a UCLA-affiliated contemporary art museum in Westwood, Los Angeles, founded by Armand Hammer and opened in November 1990. Since a 1994 partnership agreement, it has been operated by UCLA, absorbing the collections of the Wight Art Gallery and the Grunwald Center for the Graphic Arts as well as the Franklin D. Murphy Sculpture Garden. Directors have included Henry Hopkins, Ann Philbin (1999–2024), and current director Zoë Ryan (from 2025). The museum is known for its Made in L.A. biennial, the ongoing Hammer Projects series, and an active calendar of lectures, film, and public programs. Admission is free.",
